-- title:
--   Polynomial evaluation kernel at a nilpotent scalar perturbation
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $A$ a commutative ring, and $\phi:K\to A$ a unital ring homomorphism. Suppose $x\in A$, $z\in K$ and $d\in\mathbb N$ satisfy $(x-\phi(z))^d=0$. Let $n$ be the nilpotency class of $x-\phi(z)$, the least natural number whose power is zero. Write $E:K[T]\to A$ for polynomial evaluation at $x$ with coefficients mapped through $\phi$.
--
--   Then $n\le d$, and for every polynomial $q\in K[T]$,
--   $$
--   E(q)=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad (T-z)^n\mid q.
--   $$
--   Consequently
--   $$
--   \ker E=((T-z)^n).
--   $$
--   There is an injective unital ring homomorphism
--   $$
--   \overline E:K[T]/((T-z)^n)\longrightarrow A
--   $$
--   such that $\overline E([q])=E(q)$ for every polynomial $q$.
--
--   The statement includes the zero polynomial. The ring $A$ need not be nonzero or finite dimensional. In the zero ring, $n=0$ and the quotient is also the zero ring. The map is asserted to be injective; its image consists of polynomial evaluations at $x$.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission. Reuses the proved private theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_nilpotent_root_order (35842a99-e337-40f6-94fb-0afee3b6109d), accepted proof 6e1691f0-59e6-426f-ac0d-97189dcc84ee. Further ingredients at Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474 are nilpotencyClass and pow_nilpotencyClass in RingTheory/Nilpotent/Defs.lean, lines 62-81; Polynomial.le_rootMultiplicity_iff in Algebra/Polynomial/Div.lean, lines 712-721; and RingHom.lift_injective_of_ker_le_ideal in RingTheory/Ideal/Quotient/Operations.lean, lines 48-56. Sources: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/Div.lean#L712-L721 and https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474/Mathlib/RingTheory/Ideal/Quotient/Operations.lean#L48-L56. The evaluation kernel is the ideal generated by (T-z)^n, where n is the nilpotency class of x-phi(z), and evaluation induces an injective ring map from the corresponding quotient. This calculation is derived here, not quoted from the article. No new definitions; the target ring may be trivial and need not be finite dimensional.

import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Nilpotent.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_nilpotent_evaluation_kernel
    (K A : Type*) [Field K] [CommRing A]
    (φ : K →+* A) (x : A) (z : K) (d : ℕ) (hx : (x - φ z) ^ d = 0) :
    let n := nilpotencyClass (x - φ z)
    n ≤ d ∧
      (∀ q : Polynomial K, q.eval₂ φ x = 0 ↔
        (Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C z) ^ n ∣ q) ∧
      RingHom.ker (Polynomial.eval₂RingHom φ x) =
        Ideal.span ({(Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C z) ^ n} : Set (Polynomial K)) ∧
      ∃ f : (Polynomial K ⧸ Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C z) ^ n}) →+* A,
        Function.Injective f ∧ ∀ q : Polynomial K,
          f (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C z) ^ n}) q) =
            q.eval₂ φ x := by sorry
